issues.problem:
Glass/transmission is a user requirement, but it has no spec. M3 schedules glass 'per the glass spec'. M4 meanwhile freezes the interfaces glass must fit into:
- 2-bit lobe codes {D, S, NEE, NONE};
- the rc predicate D_k/R_k/F_k/I_k, defined only for reflection lobes;
- T3-4 case coverage, which has no transmission case;
- lobe-joint pdfs with no reflect/refract selection probability.
No report covers transmission: gap-bsdf sets transmission = 0, and gap-rc and gap-light never mention it. When glass lands after M4, rc.wgsl and the reservoir format need rework. Reconnection through rough glass is also an unguarded bias source, because the new direction can flip between the reflection and transmission hemispheres. Finally, the interactive default of 2 bounces (≤ 3 scattering vertices) only just covers a glass sphere, and TIR rims render dark.

